","gloss":"of"}],"gloss":"of the festival"},{"surface":"நெடியோன்","parts":[{"text":"நெடியோன்","lemma":"நெடியோன்","gloss":"the tall one / great ancestor"}],"gloss":"the tall one / great ancestor","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நன்னீர்ப்","parts":[{"text":"நல்","lemma":"நன்மை","gloss":"good"},{"text":"நீர்","lemma":"நீர்","gloss":"water"},{"text":"ப்","lemma":"ப்","gloss":"sandhi"}],"gloss":"of good water"},{"surface":"பஃறுளி","parts":[{"text":"பஃறுளி","lemma":"பஃறுளி","gloss":"Pahruḷi river"}],"gloss":"Pahruḷi river"},{"surface":"மணலினும்","parts":[{"text":"மணல்","lemma":"மணல்","gloss":"sand"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"than"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"even"}],"gloss":"than the sand"},{"surface":"பலவே","parts":[{"text":"பல","lemma":"பல","gloss":"many"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"many indeed"}]}],"literal":"Cows, and cow-natured Brahmin people and / women, and those with illness, and those who cherish / and perform the rare duties to the dwellers of the southern region, / and those who have not obtained sons like gold, / 'Our arrow we will shoot swiftly, reach your fortress!' saying, / with valor of resolve that declares the path of righteousness, / casting shade on the banner-filled sky from high above the killer male elephant, / may our king live long, Kudumi! Their king, / who gave pure gold of red lustre to the bards, / the great ancestor of the ocean festival, / may his days be more than the sand of the good-watered Pahruḷi river!","translation":"Cows, Brahmins of gentle cow-like nature, women, those suffering from illness, and those who have not yet begotten precious gold-like sons to perform the sacred rites for ancestors dwelling in the southern realm—to all of them, he proclaims: 'We are about to shoot our swift arrows, so seek refuge in your fortresses!' Such is his righteous valor. Riding high upon his killer war-elephant, casting a shadow upon the banner-filled sky, may our king Kudumi live long! He, the descendant of the great ancient king who established the festival of the ocean and gifted pure, red-lustred gold to the bards, may his years of life be even more numerous than the sands of the beautiful Pahruḷi river of pure waters!","modern":"பசுக்களும், பசு போன்ற சாந்த குணம் கொண்ட அந்தணர்களும், பெண்களும், நோயாளிகளும், தென்புலத்தில் வாழும் முன்னோர்களுக்குச் செய்ய வேண்டிய அரிய கடமைகளைச் செய்வதற்குப் பொன்னைப் போன்ற புதல்வர்களைப் பெறாதவர்களும் ஆகிய நீங்கள் அனைவரும், 'நாங்கள் எம் அம்புகளை விரைந்து செலுத்தப் போகிறோம்; உங்களது பாதுகாப்பான அரண்களைச் சென்றடையுங்கள்' என்று அறநெறி கூறும் கொள்கையுடைய வீரத்தோடு, கொலைத் தொழில் புரியும் ஆண் யானையின் மீது ஏறி, கொடிகள் பறக்கும் வானத்தை நிழலிடச் செய்யும் எம் அரசன் குடுமி பல்லாண்டு வாழ்க! பாணர்களுக்குச் செந்நிற ஒளியுடைய பசும்பொன்னை வாரி வழங்கியவனும், கடல் விழாவைக் கொண்டாடிய நெடியோன் என்னும் முன்னோனின் வழிவந்தவனுமாகிய அவனது வாழ்நாட்கள், நல்ல நீரையுடைய பஃறுளி ஆற்றின் மணலை விடப் பலவாக நீடிக்குமாக!","explanation":"The poet Neṭṭimaiyār praises the Pāṇṭiyaṉ king Palyākacālai Mutukuṭumipperuvaḻuti for his righteous conduct in warfare. Before launching an attack, the king sends out a warning to vulnerable groups—cows, gentle Brahmins, women, the sick, and those without sons to perform ancestral rites—urging them to seek safety in fortresses. This demonstrates that even in the heat of war, the king strictly adheres to the code of righteousness (aṟam). The poet then praises the king's lineage, tracing him back to Neṭiyōṉ, the ancestor who established the ocean festival, and his immense generosity in gifting pure gold to bards. Finally, she blesses the king to live for more years than the sands of the ancient, pure-watered Pahruḷi river.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,0.8],[0.8,1.0],[1.0,1.4],[1.4,2.7],[2.7,3.2],[3.2,3.6],[3.6,3.8],[3.8,4.53],[4.53,5.4],[5.4,6.3],[6.3,6.7],[6.7,7.7],[7.7,8.5],[8.5,8.7],[8.7,8.9],[8.9,10.3],[10.3,10.6],[10.6,11.2],[11.2,11.4],[11.4,12.0],[12.0,12.9],[12.9,13.2],[13.2,1